#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179512 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c91d51f-39b4-547a-971b-9c2dada9eb47" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Simple Sums Over Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/id #uuid "2574b91a-6534-562b-b4dc-8d95fd19e169" :question/math-academy-id "e-9480" :question/problem "Let $P= \\left\\{y_0, y_1, \\ldots, y_n\\right\\}$ be a partition of the interval $[-3, 5].$ If $\\Delta y_j = y_j - y_{j-1},$ calculate $\\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^n {3}\\Delta y_j.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the factor $3$ outside the summation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}3Δ{y}_{j}=3{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $\\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^n \\Delta y_j$ is just the length of the interval $[-3, 5],$ because\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j} & =Δ{y}_{1}+Δ{y}_{2}+Δ{y}_{3}+⋯+Δ{y}_{n} \\\\  & =({y}_{1}-{y}_{0})+({y}_{2}-{y}_{1})+({y}_{3}-{y}_{2})+⋯+({y}_{n}-{y}_{n-1}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{y}_{1}}-{y}_{0})+(\\cancel{{y}_{2}}-\\cancel{{y}_{1}})+(\\cancel{{y}_{3}}-\\cancel{{y}_{2}})+⋯+({y}_{n}-\\cancel{{y}_{n-1}}) \\\\  & =-{y}_{0}+{y}_{n} \\\\  & ={y}_{n}-{y}_{0} \\\\  & =5-(-3) \\\\  & =5+3 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{3}\\sum_{j=1}^n \\Delta y_j = 3 \\cdot 8 = 24.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179513 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f55bdc9-4066-5786-bafe-c3fdc96a06c9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Sums Over Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/id #uuid "8f09771b-3e0d-567b-a39f-f877bff53372" :question/math-academy-id "e-9481" :question/problem "Let $P = \\left\\{x_0, x_1, \\ldots, x_m\\right\\}$ be a partition of the interval $[-3, 4].$ If $\\Delta x_i = x_i - x_{i-1},$ calculate $\\displaystyle\\sum_{i=1}^m (x_i + x_{i-1})\\Delta x_i .$" :question/worked-solution "We can simplify the given summation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})Δ{x}_{1}+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})Δ{x}_{2}+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})Δ{x}_{m} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})({x}_{m}-{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})+({x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{m-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}}-{x}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}^{2}+{x}_{m}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $x_0 = -3$ and $x_m = 4$ are the endpoints of our partition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={4}^{2}-(-3)^{2} \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179515 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2bc800b0-3901-5154-81ac-1ef853017320" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/id #uuid "eff8c72f-429d-583a-aa22-f7786f09262a" :question/math-academy-id "e-9484" :question/problem "Which of the following are partitions of the real interval $[1,9]?$\n\n- $\\{1, 4, 5, 8\\}$\n\n- $\\{1, 3, 4, 9\\}$\n\n- $1 <     2  <    9$" :question/worked-solution "A partition $P$ of a closed interval $[a,b]$ is a finite sequence of real numbers taken from $[a,b]$ such that\n\n$$\na = x_0 <      x_1<      x_2 <      \\ldots <      x_n = b\\,.\n$$\n\nWe can express $P$ using set notation as\n\n$$\nP=\\{x_0,x_1,\\ldots,x_n\\}.\n$$\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement:\n\n- Statement I is not a partition of $[1,9]$ since it does not include the right endpoint $b=9.$\n\n- Statement II is a partition of $[1,9].$\n\n- Statement III is a partition of $[1,9].$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179905 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c91d51f-39b4-547a-971b-9c2dada9eb47" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Simple Sums Over Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d630d77c-ba48-5a29-9e49-615ab8a60c89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177431} {:answer/id #uuid "d9c8a090-99a6-5a38-acd0-7319d2aa1106" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177432} {:answer/id #uuid "dcfbd0c4-6884-5d34-a4aa-304e050de0ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177433} {:answer/id #uuid "f9cc3e2e-3a9a-5256-b0c7-ed3e9a6445ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177434} {:answer/id #uuid "73c6868a-f309-523e-ae0f-0313cf018f96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177435}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73c6868a-f309-523e-ae0f-0313cf018f96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177435} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba8d702a-61f0-5e7f-b492-21deeefab745" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177430}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bd1432fb-079c-5b39-aa64-1524227d0162" :question/math-academy-id "q-122848" :question/problem "Let $P={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}}$ be a partition of the interval $[0,3].$ If $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}5Δ{x}_{i}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple rule, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}5Δ{x}_{i}=5{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}$ is just the length of the interval $[0,3],$ because\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})+({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})+({x}_{3}-{x}_{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}-{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}}-{x}_{0})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}})+(\\cancel{{x}_{3}}-\\cancel{{x}_{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}+{x}_{m} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}-{x}_{0} \\\\  & =3-0 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n5{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}=5\\cdot 3=15.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179906 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f55bdc9-4066-5786-bafe-c3fdc96a06c9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Sums Over Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b51b1a7d-4b6c-5b32-8ec3-77de9d54c06c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177437} {:answer/id #uuid "c8e51708-97d7-5d30-8c2d-5fe611e7ae5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177438} {:answer/id #uuid "2e3cb266-f015-5a6c-b931-45c78c052755" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177439} {:answer/id #uuid "67eab901-cece-5110-bf16-72b4629d241d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177440} {:answer/id #uuid "72d394aa-ebad-5603-a14a-bd2ac5f226a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177441}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c8e51708-97d7-5d30-8c2d-5fe611e7ae5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177438} :answer-field/id #uuid "5cfe064a-e03e-540b-9a36-22d5434afef9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177436}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3d3d4439-66c9-5ffc-a015-2454a6d340fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-122849" :question/problem "Let $P={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}}$ be a partition of the interval $[0,2].$ If $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}.$" :question/worked-solution "We can simplify the given summation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})Δ{x}_{1}+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})Δ{x}_{2}+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})Δ{x}_{n} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})({x}_{m}-{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})+({x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{m-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}}-{x}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}^{2}+{x}_{m}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since ${x}_{0}=0$ and ${x}_{m}=2$ are the endpoints of our partition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={2}^{2}-{0}^{2} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186374395 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2bc800b0-3901-5154-81ac-1ef853017320" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40293fdb-f0b0-5105-8166-5fa2eec997ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374397} {:answer/id #uuid "705e3f09-0324-5d64-b4d3-c4b01cd4d956" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the statements give a partition of  $[-4,6]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374398} {:answer/id #uuid "41ec46a2-2751-59e3-aa6d-66be9ef35514" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374399} {:answer/id #uuid "0a9dc897-08ac-5e0e-ad55-9c020ba9dba0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374400} {:answer/id #uuid "a60f3b0c-0e26-5f1f-8463-4b87d25bc368" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374401}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "705e3f09-0324-5d64-b4d3-c4b01cd4d956" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the statements give a partition of  $[-4,6]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374398} :answer-field/id #uuid "f39795d1-aea8-5b4e-af92-aa80c6697c45" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374396}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d62099c6-5c34-55aa-ad1f-5500db9aeb0d" :question/math-academy-id "q-122932" :question/problem "Which of the following are partitions of the real interval $[-4,6]?$\n\n- $-5<-4<-2<0<4<6$\n- ${-3,3,5,6}$\n- ${-4,4,5}$" :question/worked-solution "A partition $P$ of a closed interval $[a,b]$ is a finite sequence of real numbers taken from $[a,b]$ such that\n\n$$\na={x}_{0}<{x}_{1}<{x}_{2}<…<{x}_{n}=b\\,.\n$$\n\nWe can express $P$ using set notation as\n\n$$\nP={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement:\n\n- Statement I is not a partition of $[-4,6]$ since $-5$ does not belong to $[-4,6].$\n\n- Statement II is not a partition of $[-4,6]$ since it does not include the left endpoint $a=-4.$\n\n- Statement III is not a partition of  $[-4,6]$ since it does not include the right endpoint $b=6.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements give a partition of  $[-4,6].$\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186374402 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2bc800b0-3901-5154-81ac-1ef853017320" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Partitions of the Real Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24bd9553-b50a-5cbb-9b58-c728e387d1a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374404} {:answer/id #uuid "1c2dac9f-c3c2-5953-9e6b-8adcd330e2c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374405} {:answer/id #uuid "260af6ac-ccad-5102-ac1c-